WEBVTT

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:14.230
Say, is it just me, or did we 
already pass by here?

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:16.640
I guess we might be lost.

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:19.850
What?! Get it together, Captain!

00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:22.150
The map didn't say anything about a forest!

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:25.790
I hate this! It's hot, and it's dark, 
and this thing is heavy!

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:27.500
I want out of these woods <i>now</i>!

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:29.070
Just drive the Kitetsu Mount!

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:31.270
Why don't you drive it yourself, then?!

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:36.640
I wanna do it!

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:41.930
I wanna try driving!

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:46.680
You guys better not let go, okay?

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:48.890
I'm serious!

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:52.680
It's pretty scary without any help 
in the early stages.

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:53.590
I know, right?

00:00:53.590 --> 00:00:55.860
Let's spook him by letting go
 when he's not paying attention!

00:00:57.750 --> 00:00:59.020
Keep it quiet!

00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:02.340
<i>I think they've both settled 
down some. That's a relief.</i>

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:03.830
Are you ready?

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:04.750
Careful now.

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:06.200
Don't let him notice...

00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:09.710
<i>I'll play along for now.</i>

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:11.840
You guys better not let go!

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:13.790
I mean it!

00:01:13.790 --> 00:01:16.190
You <i>can't</i> let go of me!

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:18.250
Huh...

00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:23.220
All right, maybe you can actually let go now.

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:30.480
<b>Green Oni
Octopus Jars</b>

00:01:30.670 --> 00:01:32.690
Help, Musashi!

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:35.780
Kojiro! Tsugumi!

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:42.570
There's someone else, too!

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:49.370
These oni never get any less monstrous.

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:50.460
But now...

00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:55.170
I'm not helpless against them anymore!

00:01:57.070 --> 00:01:59.020
Enma's Oodachi!

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:33.020
<b>Where This Road Leads</b>

00:03:35.010 --> 00:03:36.530
Where's its horn?

00:03:39.350 --> 00:03:40.060
There!

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:09.100
Kojiro! Tsugumi! You okay?

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:12.820
I'm soaked...

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:15.030
Yeah, we're okay.

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:16.270
Nice save.

00:04:17.050 --> 00:04:18.420
Thank goodness.

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:19.980
Oh, yeah...

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:22.670
Huh? It caught someone else?

00:04:22.670 --> 00:04:24.450
Hey! You okay in there?

00:04:27.290 --> 00:04:29.070
No answer...

00:04:29.070 --> 00:04:30.170
Don't tell me...

00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:31.920
They were moving a second ago!

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:34.100
They've gotta be alive!

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:51.420
<i>It's a girl.</i>

00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:54.210
Is she alive?

00:05:12.710 --> 00:05:14.150
What a relief.

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:22.330
Right here...

00:05:23.410 --> 00:05:26.020
You're bleeding.

00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:28.910
Oh, yeah.

00:05:29.510 --> 00:05:31.130
From when I saved you.

00:05:31.910 --> 00:05:35.350
You saved me?

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:36.640
Yeah.

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:40.720
I see...

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:53.270
Thank you.

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:57.280
She's gorgeous.

00:05:57.890 --> 00:06:00.380
Are you feeling okay? Any injuries?

00:06:02.530 --> 00:06:04.800
Musashi and Kojiro are gaga over her!

00:06:05.090 --> 00:06:08.250
I bet they're hearing birdsong in their heads!

00:06:08.250 --> 00:06:09.570
<i>This is great news.</i>

00:06:09.970 --> 00:06:15.440
<i>I'm still normal enough 
to think girls my age are cute.</i>

00:06:16.410 --> 00:06:19.580
<i>I need to cherish this wonderful feeling!</i>

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:23.820
Princess!

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:25.160
Princess?

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:27.910
You're all right!

00:06:28.210 --> 00:06:29.380
Chamberlain...

00:06:29.380 --> 00:06:32.180
I was ever so worried when you 
were separated from the group!

00:06:32.180 --> 00:06:36.600
Stray oni attacked me, 
and then I was saved by this man.

00:06:36.600 --> 00:06:37.700
Stray oni?

00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:42.610
Princess, I could never make it up to 
His Lordship if anything happened to you!

00:06:42.610 --> 00:06:44.700
I'm sorry, chamberlain.

00:06:45.050 --> 00:06:47.350
An actual princess...?

00:06:47.350 --> 00:06:52.390
And what exactly is a hoity-toity lady 
like that doing in the backwoods?

00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:54.010
<i>Say something like that, Musashi!</i>

00:06:54.590 --> 00:06:55.630
Actually...

00:06:58.300 --> 00:07:02.870
Sir, the princess would 
like to know your name.

00:07:02.870 --> 00:07:04.980
She should give hers first!

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:07.310
And if she has something to say,
 tell her to say it!

00:07:07.310 --> 00:07:09.520
How terribly rude of me.

00:07:11.720 --> 00:07:14.090
This is the daughter of Lord Nobumitsu,

00:07:14.090 --> 00:07:17.900
head of the Saruwatari Bushi 
under the Uesugi Alliance...

00:07:17.900 --> 00:07:20.850
Milady Saruwatari Michiru.

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:23.920
<b>Saruwatari Band
 Saruwatari Michiru</b>

00:07:20.850 --> 00:07:24.320
In order to attend the battle which 
will decide the fate of the nation,

00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:27.160
we are headed to the port of Harima.

00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:32.240
A battle that's gonna decide 
the fate of the nation?

00:07:37.170 --> 00:07:39.360
This thing is a Kitetsu Mount, too?!

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:40.900
Is this your first time riding one like it?

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:44.470
Consider the lift a token of gratitude
for Sir Musashi saving the princess.

00:07:44.470 --> 00:07:47.160
We'll clear through the 
forest in no time at all.

00:07:47.160 --> 00:07:49.740
It's great that we got a ride, huh, Musashi?

00:07:50.590 --> 00:07:51.800
Musashi?

00:07:51.800 --> 00:07:53.330
Huh? Yeah.

00:07:57.600 --> 00:07:59.750
<i>She seems like a totally different person.</i>

00:08:00.130 --> 00:08:01.990
<i>What's she upset about?</i>

00:08:03.850 --> 00:08:05.340
What is that?

00:08:06.190 --> 00:08:08.950
Musashi, check it out! 
It's crazy over there!

00:08:09.400 --> 00:08:10.620
Yeah...

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:13.180
<i>Are you guys seriously not noticing this?</i>

00:08:13.450 --> 00:08:16.670
<i>This awkward, chilly mood that's crept over?</i>

00:08:17.670 --> 00:08:20.820
<i>I can't stand this kind of atmosphere.</i>

00:08:20.820 --> 00:08:23.420
<i>So I've gotta find a way to break the ice!</i>

00:08:23.720 --> 00:08:27.730
Y'know, we were actually kind of lost!

00:08:27.730 --> 00:08:30.410
I'm so glad you have a map of the forest.

00:08:31.920 --> 00:08:33.470
<i>Come on, gimme something!</i>

00:08:33.470 --> 00:08:36.960
Huh? What's this blacked out part?

00:08:37.380 --> 00:08:38.580
Maybe a misprint?

00:08:38.580 --> 00:08:40.810
But it's the whole area...

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:43.410
<i>They're hijacking the conversation!</i>

00:08:43.410 --> 00:08:45.960
So, where are you from?

00:08:46.310 --> 00:08:49.440
<i>Talking about your hometown 
is a classic conversation starter!</i>

00:08:56.090 --> 00:08:59.930
Well, we're actually from Bicchu.

00:09:00.240 --> 00:09:01.710
<i>Another interloper!</i>

00:09:01.710 --> 00:09:05.150
By the way, you mentioned you 
were headed to the Harima port.

00:09:05.320 --> 00:09:09.940
Correct. Lord Uesugi has called for a 
gathering in order to slay a Kishin,

00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:14.280
so the Bushi of the Uesugi Alliance 
are reporting to Harima.

00:09:14.680 --> 00:09:17.190
You're headed to fight a Kishin, then?

00:09:17.580 --> 00:09:19.720
What kind of fighting style do you use?

00:09:20.220 --> 00:09:23.370
<i>If she's a Bushi, she's gotta
love talking about swords!</i>

00:09:26.160 --> 00:09:28.170
What's the Uesugi Alliance?

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:31.940
Oh, it's a network of friendly Bushi bands.

00:09:31.940 --> 00:09:35.160
Hey, could you guys not change the 
subject every few seconds?!

00:09:35.160 --> 00:09:35.930
What was that for?!

00:09:35.930 --> 00:09:38.780
I'm trying to talk to Michiru!

00:09:41.890 --> 00:09:45.630
You remembered my name...?

00:09:49.150 --> 00:09:53.290
These game trails can be quite bumpy!

00:09:59.210 --> 00:10:00.350
Musashi!

00:10:01.650 --> 00:10:02.710
Huh?

00:10:07.060 --> 00:10:08.760
Crap, this is bad!

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:21.730
Kitetsu Blade: Lapis Lazuli Lotus.

00:10:22.240 --> 00:10:23.310
You...

00:10:28.040 --> 00:10:30.100
Whoa, we're flying!

00:10:31.840 --> 00:10:34.170
Your Kitetsu Blade is awesome!

00:10:36.680 --> 00:10:38.660
You remind me of my father.

00:10:39.350 --> 00:10:42.450
When I could first use a Kitetsu Blade,

00:10:42.990 --> 00:10:45.790
he praised me just like that.

00:10:46.110 --> 00:10:47.670
You're smiling!

00:10:48.070 --> 00:10:52.270
I'm sorry I was rude before.

00:10:52.270 --> 00:10:56.800
It's okay, but... what's brought
you out of your shell all of a sudden?

00:10:57.470 --> 00:10:58.660
You won't laugh?

00:10:58.660 --> 00:10:59.640
I promise.

00:11:02.690 --> 00:11:03.940
The truth is...

00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:09.330
I'm a recluse.

00:11:11.080 --> 00:11:13.600
A recluse?

00:11:14.370 --> 00:11:17.160
It's usually just me and the chamberlain,

00:11:17.160 --> 00:11:20.200
so when there are more people...

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:23.920
I-I'm never sure how 
to join the conversation.

00:11:24.860 --> 00:11:27.080
I didn't know what to do.

00:11:27.980 --> 00:11:31.010
Is that what the issue was?

00:11:33.140 --> 00:11:34.190
You're laughing!

00:11:34.190 --> 00:11:36.810
I'm just relieved you weren't mad.

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:46.070
Say, why don't you head south with me?

00:11:46.890 --> 00:11:49.630
We're actually headed east.

00:11:50.320 --> 00:11:52.610
You won't be able to go far, then.

00:11:52.610 --> 00:11:55.150
Remember how the map was blacked out?

00:11:55.150 --> 00:11:58.080
Yeah. What's with that?

00:11:58.430 --> 00:11:59.990
It's easy enough to explain.

00:12:00.440 --> 00:12:01.950
Look. There it is.

00:12:13.840 --> 00:12:16.550
What is that?!

00:12:20.740 --> 00:12:23.160
That black wall is a Kishin.

00:12:23.520 --> 00:12:27.840
That's a Kishin? It's way too huge!

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:49.230
The wall's... moving?

00:12:50.530 --> 00:12:52.710
What the hell is this thing?!

00:12:54.050 --> 00:13:02.020
They say it was the first oni to appear 
in Hinomoto over 150 years ago.

00:13:04.960 --> 00:13:07.830
Long ago in Hinomoto...

00:13:14.070 --> 00:13:17.720
A lone oni appeared.

00:13:26.310 --> 00:13:28.120
It was extremely powerful.

00:13:29.800 --> 00:13:32.690
No human could stand against it.

00:13:34.690 --> 00:13:37.330
Hinomoto was split in two

00:13:38.100 --> 00:13:42.060
between those who saw the oni as enemies 
 and declared all-out war on them,

00:13:42.790 --> 00:13:46.760
and those who heralded the oni as gods
 and decided to worship them.

00:13:47.570 --> 00:13:51.230
The latter would go on to build mining towns,

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:55.730
where ore was harvested 
and offered up to the Kishin.

00:13:56.370 --> 00:14:00.790
As it consumed ore, it grew ever bigger,

00:14:01.160 --> 00:14:06.080
to the point that it now covers 
over half of Hinomoto.

00:14:06.600 --> 00:14:09.460
It's known as the Black Kishin.

00:14:16.050 --> 00:14:17.430
The Black Kishin...

00:14:17.740 --> 00:14:20.250
That's what we've named it.

00:14:21.030 --> 00:14:29.210
And defeating it is the unrealized ambition
 of all Bushi the past 150 years.

00:14:29.670 --> 00:14:34.190
Considering that the Black Kishin 
continues to grow with each passing day,

00:14:34.600 --> 00:14:40.260
it will eventually swallow all of Hinomoto 
if nothing is done to stop it.

00:14:40.260 --> 00:14:42.920
The entire country...?

00:14:42.920 --> 00:14:45.400
Then we need to take it out fast, right?!

00:14:45.400 --> 00:14:50.350
But an oni that no one's been
able to defeat for 150 years...

00:14:50.750 --> 00:14:53.610
I don't see how anyone can beat it now.

00:14:54.040 --> 00:15:00.620
Fear not! The leader of our alliance, 
Master Uesugi Tatsuomi, shall slay it!

00:15:00.620 --> 00:15:05.870
After all, he ranks among
 the nation's strongest Bushi,

00:15:05.870 --> 00:15:08.300
the Five Great Generals.

00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:09.750
The Five Great Generals?

00:15:09.750 --> 00:15:13.730
Yes! They are the closest anyone 
has come to unifying the nation.

00:15:13.730 --> 00:15:15.790
That sounds pretty impressive...

00:15:16.140 --> 00:15:21.950
Defeating the Kishin on Awaji Island will be
 critical to taking down the Black Kishin.

00:15:22.500 --> 00:15:26.660
I recommend you all join us 
in Harima if you're interested.

00:15:26.660 --> 00:15:29.290
Come now, Princess. Let's be on our way.

00:15:31.290 --> 00:15:34.600
Well, I hope we meet again someday.

00:15:41.250 --> 00:15:44.870
I wonder if my sister was aware of all this...

00:15:46.890 --> 00:15:50.530
Do you think that Pops 
knew about that thing?

00:15:50.850 --> 00:15:52.370
No clue.

00:15:52.370 --> 00:15:55.800
The scrolls he left didn't mention it.

00:15:55.800 --> 00:15:57.450
Are you sure?

00:15:57.450 --> 00:15:58.820
I guess we can check.

00:16:03.000 --> 00:16:06.360
Oh, every band has these scrolls.

00:16:06.360 --> 00:16:07.640
What? Really?

00:16:07.640 --> 00:16:12.420
Yeah. It has a record of the 
Kishin's names and traits.

00:16:12.770 --> 00:16:15.590
If this is something all Bushi bands carry...

00:16:15.590 --> 00:16:17.910
then why'd my dad have it?

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:22.130
I mean, it probably means he 
was a Bushi in a band, right?

00:16:22.380 --> 00:16:23.470
Right?

00:16:24.340 --> 00:16:27.120
Then Pops really did have connections 
to the outside world...

00:16:27.120 --> 00:16:29.960
Hey, this scroll has a seal.

00:16:30.260 --> 00:16:31.230
What seal?

00:16:31.230 --> 00:16:32.540
It's for identification.

00:16:32.940 --> 00:16:35.680
Let's see, from the looks of it...

00:16:36.200 --> 00:16:38.650
This is the seal of the lord of the Uesugi.

00:16:38.650 --> 00:16:40.150
Isn't that...

00:16:40.370 --> 00:16:45.350
It probably means Kojiro's dad 
belonged to the Uesugi Band.

00:17:08.130 --> 00:17:11.080
Everyone here is part of 
the Uesugi Alliance?!

00:17:11.080 --> 00:17:12.340
Wow!

00:17:12.340 --> 00:17:14.910
Why are we way out on the fringe?

00:17:14.910 --> 00:17:17.940
Well, the Amako band is pretty minor.

00:17:17.940 --> 00:17:21.470
Near the center are the Arima,
 the Ootomo, and...

00:17:22.470 --> 00:17:26.430
The second-biggest band in the 
Uesugi Alliance, the Shimazu!

00:17:29.650 --> 00:17:33.810
Our duty is to slay the 
Kishin of Awaji Island.

00:17:34.330 --> 00:17:35.920
Let's take the island back!

00:17:35.920 --> 00:17:36.860
Right!

00:17:38.850 --> 00:17:42.240
Natsuki, do you remember what Father said?

00:17:42.240 --> 00:17:47.740
Yeah. Whoever takes the Kishin's horn on 
Awaji gets to be the head of the clan, right?

00:17:47.740 --> 00:17:50.040
I'm sure Sir Akihiro can do it.

00:17:57.990 --> 00:17:59.430
Get in line!

00:17:59.660 --> 00:18:02.880
First come, first serve. No cutting.

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:04.390
We're waiting back here!

00:18:02.880 --> 00:18:04.390
Try and calm down.

00:18:04.700 --> 00:18:08.270
I hate it when anything is out of place...

00:18:08.270 --> 00:18:10.860
You're a little <i>too</i> organized, 
Master Kanetatsu.

00:18:16.080 --> 00:18:18.980
<i>My lord! There are reports that
 the Obsidian Goddess was spotted</i>

00:18:18.980 --> 00:18:20.710
<i>at the great eastern mine of Mimasaka.</i>

00:18:20.920 --> 00:18:23.490
<i>Word came from one of 
the bands under our authority.</i>

00:18:26.290 --> 00:18:28.310
The Obsidian Goddess...

00:18:30.090 --> 00:18:35.210
Come on, Tatsuomi.
 I don't actually work for you.

00:18:43.150 --> 00:18:44.860
I bought a lot of stuff.

00:18:45.130 --> 00:18:47.590
I wonder if Master will be happy.

00:18:48.840 --> 00:18:51.000
I guess snacks wouldn't really please him.

00:18:51.280 --> 00:18:54.580
Maybe I should have hunted 
down a Kitetsu Blade...

00:18:54.860 --> 00:18:58.470
No, no! I'm off duty after
finishing up a mission.

00:18:58.470 --> 00:19:01.030
And I don't believe in working without pay.

00:19:07.580 --> 00:19:08.780
Ugh...

00:19:12.160 --> 00:19:14.370
No one should come around here.

00:19:19.130 --> 00:19:21.060
H-Hey, Nanao...

00:19:22.250 --> 00:19:25.030
<i>Looks like you're relaxing off duty, huh?</i>

00:19:25.410 --> 00:19:28.210
Everyone being able to keep tabs 
on you isn't very relaxing...

00:19:28.270 --> 00:19:36.190
<b>The Obsidian Eight</b>

00:19:28.440 --> 00:19:31.980
<i>We all have the same stones within us.</i>

00:19:31.980 --> 00:19:34.460
<i>That lets us know what's going on, 
no matter the distance.</i>

00:19:34.460 --> 00:19:39.640
Speaking of duty, I hear you actually 
found the Obsidian Goddess.

00:19:39.640 --> 00:19:42.600
Yes. The genuine article this time.

00:19:42.600 --> 00:19:44.110
There's no doubt about it.

00:19:44.110 --> 00:19:45.740
<i></i>I<i> found her!</i>

00:19:45.740 --> 00:19:48.000
<i>I heard she rejected you.</i>

00:19:48.000 --> 00:19:50.490
<i>Wanna go drown your sorrows? My treat.</i>

00:19:50.490 --> 00:19:52.950
<i>What, you wanna go drinking, Seiroku?</i>

00:19:52.950 --> 00:19:55.630
<i>I'm trying to say I'm worried about you!</i>

00:19:55.040 --> 00:20:00.520
Seiroku, consideration and other delicate 
sentiments don't apply to my master.

00:20:01.060 --> 00:20:04.590
<i>We need to keep the Obsidian Goddess 
out of Bushi hands.</i>

00:20:05.440 --> 00:20:09.310
<i>The compass would show the 
way to divine treasures.</i>

00:20:10.050 --> 00:20:15.120
<i>Our duty is to ensure the survival of the 
Kishin so that we can live alongside them.</i>

00:20:15.430 --> 00:20:17.030
<i>Let us all work together, 
brothers and sisters.</i>

00:20:17.030 --> 00:20:18.100
<i>Right.</i>

00:20:18.100 --> 00:20:20.240
<i>Let's go and grab her right now!</i>

00:20:20.630 --> 00:20:24.190
<i>I think it'd be a good idea to send 
someone who can approach in secret.</i>

00:20:24.190 --> 00:20:28.900
<i>Yeah, if we send someone without 
a plan, she'll get away. Again.</i>

00:20:29.130 --> 00:20:32.730
<i>I-If I clean up the mess that Nanao made...</i>

00:20:32.730 --> 00:20:35.370
<i>Will I get praised for it?</i>

00:20:35.370 --> 00:20:36.540
So creepy!

00:20:37.140 --> 00:20:39.600
<i>You wanna show off to Nanao, don't you?</i>

00:20:39.600 --> 00:20:43.810
<i>M-Maybe I should go this time...</i>

00:20:45.840 --> 00:20:48.420
We're almost at the port of Harima.

00:20:48.420 --> 00:20:49.780
We'll be able to see the ocean.

00:20:49.780 --> 00:20:51.580
The ocean, huh?

00:20:51.580 --> 00:20:52.600
The ocean...

00:20:52.920 --> 00:20:55.070
Do you guys even know what an ocean is?

00:20:55.070 --> 00:20:56.330
Sure we do.

00:20:56.330 --> 00:20:58.360
During the Sengoku period,

00:20:57.610 --> 00:21:04.030
<b>Ocean of Blood</b>

00:20:58.360 --> 00:21:02.980
the ocean was a body of water that was turned
red with the blood of innocent farmers.

00:21:04.270 --> 00:21:06.300
Your school was really full of it, huh?

00:21:06.300 --> 00:21:09.000
I wonder what the ocean's really like...

00:21:10.680 --> 00:21:12.190
Should be exciting, huh, Kojiro?

00:21:13.830 --> 00:21:17.660
You guys really don't mind 
me being selfish like this?

00:21:17.660 --> 00:21:19.440
It's not selfish, man.

00:21:19.440 --> 00:21:22.820
It's only natural to want to 
know more about your family.

00:21:22.820 --> 00:21:26.640
Yeah. Besides, I wanna 
know more about Pops myself.

00:21:29.910 --> 00:21:33.770
I need to know more about him, too.

00:21:33.770 --> 00:21:39.150
I never even thought about 
where he came from before.

00:21:39.560 --> 00:21:43.780
But if we go to the Uesugi, 
we might be able to learn something.

00:21:47.760 --> 00:21:49.290
What's that smell?

00:21:52.630 --> 00:21:54.500
I think we're coming up on something.

00:21:54.900 --> 00:21:56.170
That's the ocean!

00:21:59.460 --> 00:22:01.510
That's the ocean?

00:22:01.800 --> 00:22:02.930
It's so blue!

00:23:37.060 --> 00:23:39.930
<b>The Battle of Awaji Island Starts Summer 2022</b>

00:23:37.440 --> 00:23:39.440
This is Harima?!
